  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">INDIGENOUS GREAT GREEN MACAW SANCTUARY IN LA MOSKITIA, HONDURAS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO CONTINUE SUPPORTING A CONSERVATION EFFORT LED BY 11 INDIGENOUS COMMUNITIES IN THE REMOTE MOSKITIA REGION OF HONDURAS BY SUSTAINING PATROLS AND ESTABLISHING A BIRD SANCTUARY. THE PROJECT IS INTENDED TO CONSERVE THE CRITICALLY ENDANGERED GREAT GREEN MACAW (ARA AMBIGUOUS) BY ADDRESSING THE IMPACTS OF POACHING AND HABITAT DESTRUCTION. SPECIFIC ACTIVITIES INCLUDE: (1) MEASURING THE BASELINE POPULATION OF GREAT GREEN MACAWS (GGM) AND DOCUMENTING CURRENT ACTIVE NESTS IN THE REGION TO BETTER UNDERSTAND POPULATION DYNAMICS (2) CONSTRUCTING A RANGER STATION, TRAILS, AND MONITORING KIOSK FOR MONITORING AND PATROLLING ACTIVITIES, AS WELL AS FOR ECOTOURISM AND EDUCATIONAL ACTIVITIES THAT WILL PROVIDE ECONOMIC OPPORTUNITIES FOR LOCALS (3) COORDINATING WITH THE HONDURAN ARMY TO PATROL WEEKLY DURING NESTING SEASON TO DISSUADE POACHERS FROM ENTERING THE AREA (5) IN COORDINATION WITH LOCAL VILLAGES AND THE TERRITORIAL COUNCIL, DEVELOPING A GGM SANCTUARY ON PUBLIC LAND THAT WILL PROTECT GGMS AND PROVIDE A PLACE FOR EDUCATION AND ECOTOURISM AND (6) STRENGTHENING LOCAL CAPACITY TO MANAGE THE PROJECT BY PARTNERING WITH THE FOUNDATION FOR ECOSYSTEM AND BIODIVERSITY RESEARCH AND CONSERVATION TO PROMOTE PROJECT SUSTAINABILITY.</narrative>
  </description>
